Schröder's fondness for Russia has drawn controversy, particularly since the Russian invasion of Ukraine in 2022.&#160;
Schröder's&#160;tax-payer financed Berlin office was closed in 2022 over his involvement in the Russian energy sector, and he has also faced calls by fellow party members to be expelled from the SPD.
Schröder, however, has survived the attempt&#160;to be kicked out of his party.
